WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:05.432
Scrooge quickly realized that he hadn't traveled very far this time.

2
00:00:05.433 --> 00:00:10.008
He was standing with the Ghost of Christmas Present in a different part of London.

3
00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:15.769
A church bell was striking the time—one in the afternoon.

4
00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:21.444
Again, as Scrooge looked around, he saw people enjoying the day.

5
00:00:21.445 --> 00:00:31.369
There was a man roasting chestnuts over an open fire, and people hanging garlands of holly and mistletoe.

6
00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:35.283
Carolers sang while others hummed along.

7
00:00:35.284 --> 00:00:39.895
"Why aren't any of these people working?" Scrooge muttered.

8
00:00:39.896 --> 00:00:45.363
"They're all wasting their time!"

9
00:00:45.364 --> 00:00:49.076
The ghost had stopped in front of a small meat shop.

10
00:00:49.077 --> 00:00:53.259
Scrooge joined him and peered in the window.

11
00:00:53.260 --> 00:01:00.754
"That's quite a turkey," Scrooge said, eyeing an enormous bird hanging from a hook.

12
00:01:00.755 --> 00:01:07.160
"It would take a great number of people to eat it. I wonder how much it costs."

13
00:01:07.161 --> 00:01:14.212
"Papa, look at that huge turkey!" a high-pitched voice cried out before the ghost could respond.

14
00:01:14.213 --> 00:01:18.152
Scrooge spun around and saw a familiar face.

15
00:01:18.153 --> 00:01:22.699
"Why, it's Bob Cratchit," he said in surprise.

16
00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:27.176
He squinted at the frail child sitting on his clerk's shoulder.

17
00:01:27.177 --> 00:01:32.581
The boy was waving a crutch and smiling from ear to ear.

18
00:01:32.582 --> 00:01:42.914
"And I suppose that's Tiny Tim," Scrooge said, thinking of the weak little baby he'd seen earlier.

19
00:01:42.915 --> 00:01:47.747
"It's a huge turkey indeed, my boy," Cratchit said.

20
00:01:47.748 --> 00:01:52.041
"What sort of king or emperor do you suppose might buy it?"

21
00:01:52.042 --> 00:02:00.059
Tiny Tim giggled. "I know! The queen is going to order it for the palace!

22
00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:04.150
And maybe she'll invite our whole family to dine with her.

23
00:02:04.151 --> 00:02:12.079
I bet we'll eat oyster soup and buttered potatoes and a plum pudding as big as me!"

24
00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:18.031
Cratchit chuckled, though his eyes looked rather sad.

25
00:02:18.032 --> 00:02:20.820
"That sounds wonderful, Tim.

26
00:02:20.821 --> 00:02:26.771
But how would you know which fork to use for each course?" He winked.

27
00:02:26.772 --> 00:02:32.695
"One must know such things to dine with the queen at the palace, you see."

28
00:02:32.696 --> 00:02:36.370
Tiny Tim giggled again.

29
00:02:36.371 --> 00:02:42.119
"I would just watch Her Majesty, and use the same forks that she uses."

30
00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:46.147
"Clever boy!" Cratchit said.

31
00:02:46.148 --> 00:02:50.040
He gently squeezed Tiny Tim's legs and smiled.

32
00:02:50.041 --> 00:02:53.127
"That sounds like a fine plan.

33
00:02:53.128 --> 00:03:01.152
But just in case our royal invitation doesn't arrive, your mother is planning a feast for us to enjoy later."

34
00:03:01.153 --> 00:03:05.119
"That sounds even better, Papa," Tiny Tim said.

35
00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.830
"I bet Mama is a much better cook than the queen.

36
00:03:08.831 --> 00:03:14.490
Now let's go watch the ice skaters in the park. Can we, please?"

37
00:03:14.491 --> 00:03:21.239
"Of course we can." Turning away from the shop window, Cratchit started toward the park.

38
00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:28.924
Scrooge followed with the spirit, amazed that his clerk was spending the whole day carrying his child around the city.

39
00:03:28.925 --> 00:03:34.141
Cratchit and Tiny Tim took their time in reaching the park.

40
00:03:34.142 --> 00:03:41.940
Along the way they stopped to admire the holiday decorations on houses and lampposts.

41
00:03:41.941 --> 00:03:46.067
They exclaimed over the beautiful things in the shop windows.

42
00:03:46.068 --> 00:03:50.759
They talked and laughed together about all of it.

43
00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:57.501
Scrooge shook his head. "They're having so much fun together," he thought.

44
00:03:57.502 --> 00:04:03.926
He couldn't understand their bright cheer when there was so much for the Cratchit family to worry about.

45
00:04:03.927 --> 00:04:12.648
They were not only poor but also had to concern themselves with the small boy's health.

46
00:04:12.649 --> 00:04:17.419
Finally Cratchit and Tiny Tim reached the park.

47
00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:25.269
The lake was frozen solid, and skaters were gliding over the frozen surface on ice skates.

48
00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:30.246
Tiny Tim watched the skaters for a while with a serious expression.

49
00:04:30.247 --> 00:04:34.150
"Ice skating looks like fun, Papa," he said.

50
00:04:34.151 --> 00:04:39.010
"Do you think I'll ever be strong enough to do it?"

51
00:04:39.011 --> 00:04:43.859
"I'm absolutely sure you will skate one day, son."

52
00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:52.145
Cratchit smiled, though once again, Scrooge detected a flicker of pain in his clerk's expression.

53
00:04:52.146 --> 00:04:58.916
"Now, Tim, shall we go and finish our errands?"

54
00:04:58.917 --> 00:05:03.875
This time the spirit made no move to follow Cratchit and Tiny Tim.

55
00:05:03.876 --> 00:05:06.919
So, Scrooge stayed in place too.

56
00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:10.492
He watched Cratchit wind his way through the park.

57
00:05:10.493 --> 00:05:17.679
Scrooge was unable to stop thinking about what he'd heard Cratchit say to Tiny Tim.

58
00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:23.774
"Cratchit is a fool if he thinks his son will ever be able to skate," Scrooge snapped.

59
00:05:23.775 --> 00:05:27.562
"The boy can't even walk without using his crutch!

60
00:05:27.563 --> 00:05:31.727
Why would Cratchit tell him such a thing? It's a lie!"

61
00:05:31.728 --> 00:05:39.827
"Perhaps Cratchit thinks it will make Tiny Tim happy to imagine skating," the ghost said quietly.

62
00:05:39.828 --> 00:05:45.100
"Now, come, for we have more errands to do ourselves."

63
00:05:45.101 --> 00:05:55.836
The ghost waved his arm, and the skaters and the park disappeared.

